[b]Bring two more operators into battle.[/b] Squad Six Reforged expands your squad from four to [b]six[/b] in Star Wars: Zero Company, giving you more room for your favorite squadmates and class combinations.

This is a continuation of [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/44][b]Squad Six[/b][/url] by [b]arctco[/b], shared with their permission. Most of the mod remains their work, including the original testing and hand-picked mission list. Reforged builds on that foundation with fixes for deploying the extra two operators.

[heading]What You Get[/heading]
[list]
[*][b]A squad of six.[/b] Bring two extra operators on missions that support the larger squad.[/*]
[*][b]Room for everyone on squad select.[/b] Choose all six operators and see them together in the lineup, with a nameplate for each.[/*]
[*][b]Better deployment for the extra two.[/b] Added deployment spots help them start alongside the rest of your squad, with automatic repositioning if they get stuck or left outside the deployment area.[/*]
[*][b]The same classes, abilities and equipment.[/b] Build your team using the game's existing options. Progression and enemies keep their usual rules.[/*]
[/list]

[heading]Improvements Over Squad Six 1.1.4[/heading]
[list]
[*][b]Fixes for floating, sunken or obstructed deployment spots,[/b] including problem spots in Retake Luunata, Dark Waters and The Infinite Coil.[/*]
[*][b]Better placement in tight spaces,[/b] so the extra operators can join the squad in narrow deployment areas.[/*]
[*][b]Automatic help for operators stuck at mission start.[/b] If an extra operator starts somewhere they cannot move from, the mod can place them beside a squadmate.[/*]
[*][b]Fewer interruptions during deployment.[/b] Operators are no longer repositioned just for crossing a squadmate's spot while walking in, and squads of four use the game's normal placement.[/*]
[*][b]Easier installation.[/b] Install with Vortex, Zero Mod Manager or Zero Company Mod Command, or extract the download into your game folder.[/*]
[/list]

[heading]Which Missions Support Six?[/heading]
Most missions that normally allow four operators are expanded to six. Missions that add story characters or choose your squad for you keep their usual four to avoid duplicate characters and saving problems:
[list]
[*]The Serolonis Job (the opening tutorial)[/*]
[*]Smugglers' Den[/*]
[*]Hero missions, including Buy Cheap, Never Sleep; Best Served Cold; Origin of Infection; Sisters; No Kings, No Masters; and Rescue Jae Mordant[/*]
[/list]
Solo and three-operator missions also keep their original squad limits, except Deep Cover, which now takes six. You do not need to change any settings for these exceptions.

[heading]Tested Missions[/heading]
Tested with six operators on game build [b]25134257[/b] in Retake Luunata, Dark Waters, Unfinished Business, The Infinite Coil (the finale), a crisis mission and several skirmishes. Hero missions have also been checked at their usual four.

Not every mission has been played with six yet. If you run into a problem, please report it using the details under [b]Troubleshooting[/b] below.

[heading]Requirements[/heading]
[list]
[*][b]Star Wars: Zero Company[/b][/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/9]UE4SS for Star Wars Zero Company[/url][/*]
[/list]

[heading]Compatibility[/heading]
Use only one squad-size mod at a time. Remove arctco's original [b]Squad Six[/b], [b]Squad Expansion[/b] or any other squad-size mod before installing Reforged.

[heading]Switching From Squad Six[/heading]
You can continue your existing campaign, but [b]remove the original Squad Six before installing Reforged[/b]. Mod managers treat them as separate mods and will not replace the original automatically.

Remove it through your mod manager, or delete these files by hand:
[list]
[*]The [b]ZCOMSquadSix[/b] folder in [b]Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/Mods/[/b][/*]
[*][b]pakchunk99-ZCOMSquadSix_P.pak[/b], [b]pakchunk99-ZCOMSquadSix_P.ucas[/b] and [b]pakchunk99-ZCOMSquadSix_P.utoc[/b] in [b]Content/Paks/~mods/[/b][/*]
[/list]

[heading]Installation[/heading]
[b]Install UE4SS first and close the game before installing the mod.[/b]

The download includes two required parts: [b]Squad Six Reforged[/b] and [b]Squad Six Reforged - Core[/b]. [b]Install and enable both.[/b]

[b]Mod manager[/b]
Install the ZIP with any of these:
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/29]Zero Mod Manager[/url]: choose [b]Install all components[/b].[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarszerocompany/mods/121]Zero Company Mod Command[/url]: enable both Squad Six Reforged and Squad Six Reforged - Core.[/*]
[*][b]Vortex[/b]: install it like any other mod; both parts are deployed together.[/*]
[/list]

[b]Manual installation[/b]
Extract the ZIP into your game's [b]SWZeroCompany[/b] folder, the one containing [b]Binaries[/b] and [b]Content[/b]. Allow the folders to merge:
[code]SWZeroCompany/[/code]
After extraction, you should have these two folders:
[code]SWZeroCompany/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/Mods/SquadSixReforged/
SWZeroCompany/Content/Paks/~mods/SquadSixReforged_Core/[/code]

The mod is enabled by the included [b]enabled.txt[/b]. If it does not load with your UE4SS setup, add this line to [b]Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/Mods/mods.txt[/b]:
[code]SquadSixReforged : 1[/code]
Start the game once both parts are installed.

[b]Updating[/b]
Close the game, install the new ZIP the same way, then start the game again. Use a full restart after installing or updating; UE4SS's "Reload All Mods" is not supported.

[b]Uninstalling[/b]
[b]Finish or abandon any mission in progress before removing the mod.[/b] A mission saved with six operators needs the mod to remain installed.

Close the game, then disable or remove both parts through your mod manager. For a manual uninstall, delete the two folders shown above.

[heading]Known Issues[/heading]
[list]
[*]An extra operator may briefly jump into position when an encounter starts. This is the automatic placement correction.[/*]
[*]If an operator still gets stuck at deployment, open the UE4SS console and enter [b]squadsixrescue[/b] to move stuck operators back into the deployment area.[/*]
[/list]

[heading]Troubleshooting[/heading]
Report problems in the [b]Bugs[/b] tab here on Nexus or on [url=https://github.com/chatterchats/SquadSixReforged]GitHub[/url]. Please include:
[list]
[*]The mission name and what happened[/*]
[*]Your game build and UE4SS version[/*]
[*]Your other installed mods[/*]
[*]Your [b]UE4SS.log[/b] file, found in [b]Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/[/b][/*]
[/list]
The mod's log entries start with [b][SQUAD_SIX_REFORGED][/b] and include checks to help diagnose problems after game updates. You can review the log before sharing, since it may include folder paths on your PC.

[heading]Source Code[/heading]
The source code and technical documentation are available on [url=https://github.com/chatterchats/SquadSixReforged]GitHub[/url].

